⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Calvin Miller
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Calvin Miller:C1:c079ec⟧

WHO   — Calvin Miller — the unmade Maker
WHAT  — The bent Maker — a clever, vain, corrosive young man whose real power is starved and twisted into Unmaking, the living proof that the rarest knack turns poison the moment it is turned to the self.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because he cannot bear to be less than Alvin, and will tear down sooner than build what he cannot own; because he wants the glory of Making without the labor of love; because the Unmaker offers him everything Alvin earned, for free, at the cost of his soul.
HOW   — By a Maker's sense he never disciplined — undoing seams instead of mending them, sickening flesh, gnawing at trust and craft — and by going to Europe to study Napoleon's knack of command, hunting borrowed power to fill the place where his own should have grown.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I am a Maker too — and what my brother builds with love, I will unbuild for spite.

